      "writtenOn": "2023-03-16T07:40:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "+1 to Chiachang about the location – this goes together with `KEY_MIN_UDP_PORT_4500_NAT_TIMEOUT_SEC_INT` above. It\u0027s for VPN clients and not for IWLAN, so it doesn\u0027t really make sense in the IWLAN group.\n\nAs for the hiddenness : in the foreseeable future, this value is not meant to be managed by carriers, but by the PPN team according to what they observe works best on any given carrier. There is testing in progress to find the best value for each carrier, and there are efforts in progress to communicate and continuously test what is the best value. Therefore, making it public or not makes no practical difference because carriers are not expected to touch it, at least this year. That\u0027s why we ended up with this plan to keep it private for now. I know it\u0027s a bit of a stretch, but this is what we\u0027ve been asked to do.\n\nI don\u0027t know if the PPN team will decide to continue maintaining this value for each carrier for a long time or whether they intend to eventually ask carriers to manage it – if the latter, they\u0027ll make it public.\n\nDoes this make sense ?",
      "parentUuid": "718a562d_c667d96f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4331,
